IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `adaq-dates`
IMPORT `adaq-complainant`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1991 (Qld) -- worked cases for the questions of a complainant (adaq-complainant.l4) and the
-- date helpers (adaq-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from
-- the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts and
-- dates are illustrative.
-- Day counts used: 28 days after 1 March 2027 is 29 March 2027; 28 days after 20 December 2026 is 17 January 2027; 28
-- days after 10 February 2028 (a leap year) is 9 March 2028, and after 10 February 2027 is 10 March 2027; 29 days after
-- 1 March 2027 is 30 March 2027; 1 year after 15 March 2026 is 15 March 2027, after 1 February 2026 is 1 February 2027,
-- after 1 June 2026 is 1 June 2027, and after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029; 6 months after 15 January 2027 is
-- 15 July 2027, after 31 August 2026 is 28 February 2027, after 31 August 2027 is 29 February 2028, after 15 October
-- 2026 is 15 April 2027. 9 April 2027 is a Friday; the next business day is Monday 12 April 2027.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `the date helpers`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 17 1 2027
#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2028
#ASSERT `the day` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 2 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `years after` (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `years after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 7 2027
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the same day` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 4 2027
#ASSERT `the later of` (`d` 10 4 2027) `and` (`d` 12 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 4 2027
#ASSERT `the later of` (`d` 13 4 2027) `and` (`d` 12 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 13 4 2027
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2100 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the days in month` 2 `of` 2000 EQUALS 29

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 7, 8 -- attributes`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `impairment` `I have the attribute` EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination on the basis of this attribute (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `pregnancy` `I had the attribute in the past` EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination on the basis of this attribute (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `sexuality` `the person presumed I have, or had, the attribute` EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination on the basis of this attribute (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `race` `it is a characteristic often imputed to people with the attribute` EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination on the basis of this attribute (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `impairment` `a person I am associated with, or related to, has the attribute` EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination on the basis of this attribute (ss 7, 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `another characteristic, not listed in section 7` `I have the attribute` EQUALS `no: section 7 lists the attributes the Act protects, and this is not one of them`
#ASSERT `Is the ground of my complaint a protected attribute` `age` `some other link` EQUALS `not covered: section 8 says what discrimination on the basis of an attribute includes, and this link is not one of its paragraphs`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 10, 11 -- direct and indirect discrimination`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` TRUE `it was the only reason`
#ASSERT `Was I directly discriminated against` TRUE `it was one of 2 or more reasons, and a substantial reason`
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I directly discriminated against` TRUE `it was one of 2 or more reasons, but not a substantial reason`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I directly discriminated against` TRUE `it was not a reason`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I directly discriminated against` FALSE `it was the only reason`)

#ASSERT `Was I indirectly discriminated against` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I indirectly discriminated against` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I indirectly discriminated against` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I indirectly discriminated against` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I indirectly discriminated against` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `part 4 -- areas`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `pregnancy` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `somewhere else` `race` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Act prohibits discrimination only in the areas of activity set out in chapter 2, part 4 (s 6(2)(a)(iii))`
-- a partnership of 6 people is in; 5 is out
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `being invited to become a partner, or as a partner (ss 16, 17, 18)` `sex` 6 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `being invited to become a partner, or as a partner (ss 16, 17, 18)` `sex` 5 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the partnership sections apply only to a partnership of 6 or more people (ss 16, 17, 18, 56, 57, 70, 71)`
-- goods and services: a business is in; a non-profit sporting association is out of s 46, and is not a club either (finding 1)
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `impairment` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `impairment` 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a non-profit association established for a social, literary, cultural, political, sporting, recreational, community service or similar purpose is not a supplier of goods or services (s 46(2))`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `applying to join, or as a member of, a club (ss 94, 95)` `impairment` 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: an association is a club only if it carries out its purposes for the purpose of making a profit (schedule 1, definition of club)`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `applying to join, or as a member of, a club (ss 94, 95)` `impairment` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
-- organisations: trade union activity excluded only where the IR Act provisions apply
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `joining, or as a member of, an organisation of workers, employers, or people in an industry, profession, trade or business (ss 19, 20)` `trade union activity` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: discrimination on the basis of trade union activity is excluded where the Industrial Relations Act 2016, chapter 12, part 9, division 2 or part 10 applies (ss 19(2), 20(2))`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `joining, or as a member of, an organisation of workers, employers, or people in an industry, profession, trade or business (ss 19, 20)` `trade union activity` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `joining, or as a member of, an organisation of workers, employers, or people in an industry, profession, trade or business (ss 19, 20)` `sex` 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`
-- local government: political belief excluded, sex not
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `as a member of a local government, in the performance of official functions (s 102)` `political belief or activity` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: discrimination between local government members on the basis of political belief or activity is excluded (s 102(2))`
#ASSERT `Is the area covered by the Act` `as a member of a local government, in the performance of official functions (s 102)` `sex` 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Act prohibits discrimination in this area of activity (chapter 2, part 4)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `exemptions`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `a genuine occupational requirement for the position (s 25(1))` `seeking work, or being offered work (s 14)` `sex` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `a genuine occupational requirement for the position (s 25(1))` `seeking work, or being offered work (s 14)` `sex` FALSE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `a genuine occupational requirement for the position (s 25(1))` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `sex` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination in this area of activity`
-- religious employer: s 14 or 15 only; not age, race or impairment
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `the employer's religious beliefs (s 25(3))` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `sexuality` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `the employer's religious beliefs (s 25(3))` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `race` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination on this attribute`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `the employer's religious beliefs (s 25(3))` `using an employment agency (s 23)` `sexuality` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination in this area of activity`
-- youth wages: under 21 on age only
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `youth wages (s 33)` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `age` FALSE 20 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `youth wages (s 33)` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `age` TRUE 21 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `youth wages (s 33)` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `sex` TRUE 18 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination on this attribute`
-- unjustifiable hardship: impairment only; not in the administration of State laws
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `special services or facilities, or the circumstances of an impairment, would impose unjustifiable hardship (ss 35, 36, 44, 51, 92, 100)` `applying to, or studying at, an educational institution (ss 38, 39)` `impairment` TRUE 15 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `special services or facilities, or the circumstances of an impairment, would impose unjustifiable hardship (ss 35, 36, 44, 51, 92, 100)` `applying to, or studying at, an educational institution (ss 38, 39)` `impairment` FALSE 15 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `special services or facilities, or the circumstances of an impairment, would impose unjustifiable hardship (ss 35, 36, 44, 51, 92, 100)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `age` TRUE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination on this attribute`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `special services or facilities, or the circumstances of an impairment, would impose unjustifiable hardship (ss 35, 36, 44, 51, 92, 100)` `dealing with a person administering a State law or a State Government program (s 101)` `impairment` TRUE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination in this area of activity`
-- age-based concessions
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `age-based benefits and concessions (s 49)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `age` TRUE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `age-based benefits and concessions (s 49)` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `age` TRUE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination in this area of activity`
-- shared accommodation: 3 others in, 4 out
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `shared accommodation in the main home (s 87)` `applying for, renting or living in accommodation (ss 82 to 85)` `relationship status` TRUE 30 3 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `shared accommodation in the main home (s 87)` `applying for, renting or living in accommodation (ss 82 to 85)` `relationship status` TRUE 30 4 FALSE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`
-- religious bodies: not work or education
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `a body established for religious purposes acting in accordance with its doctrine (s 109(1)(d))` `applying to, or studying at, an educational institution (ss 38, 39)` `sexuality` TRUE 16 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: this exemption does not reach discrimination in this area of activity`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `a body established for religious purposes acting in accordance with its doctrine (s 109(1)(d))` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `sexuality` TRUE 30 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
-- sport: sex restriction not for children under 12
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `restrictions on competitive sport (s 111)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `sex` TRUE 10 0 TRUE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `restrictions on competitive sport (s 111)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `sex` TRUE 14 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `restrictions on competitive sport (s 111)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `age` TRUE 10 0 TRUE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
-- general exemptions in any area
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `workplace health and safety (s 108)` `at work, as a worker (s 15)` `impairment` TRUE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `yes: the exemption applies, so the discrimination is not unlawful (the respondent must prove it, s 205)`
#ASSERT `Does the exemption apply to me` `welfare measures (s 104)` `being supplied goods or services (s 46)` `age` FALSE 40 0 FALSE EQUALS `no: the exemption's conditions are not met or not proved (s 205)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `sexual harassment`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `a remark with sexual connotations relating to me` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I sexually harassed` `an unsolicited act of physical intimacy` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I sexually harassed` `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature in relation to me` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I sexually harassed` `conduct of none of these kinds` TRUE TRUE)

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `chapter 4`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the person who encouraged it liable too` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: requesting or encouraging a contravention is itself a contravention (s 122), and as the other person acted or tried to act on it, both are jointly and severally liable for it, and you may complain against either or both (s 123)`
#ASSERT `Is the person who encouraged it liable too` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes, for the request or encouragement itself (s 122); the joint liability of s 123 does not arise, as the other person did not act or try to act on it`
#ASSERT `Is the person who encouraged it liable too` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: sections 122 and 123 reach only a person who requested or encouraged a contravention of the Act`

#ASSERT `Can I be asked for the information` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a person must not ask you to supply information on which unlawful discrimination might be based (s 124(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I be asked for the information` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the request is necessary to comply with, or specifically authorised by, an existing provision of another Act, a court order, an existing award or industrial agreement, or an order of QCAT or the industrial relations commission (s 124(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I be asked for the information` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the asker has a defence: it proves the information was reasonably required for a purpose that did not involve discrimination (s 124(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I be asked for the information` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 124 limits only requests for information on which unlawful discrimination might be based`

#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `race` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `yes: it is unlawful vilification, and you may complain about it (s 124A(1))`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `religious belief or religious activity` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `yes: it is unlawful vilification, and you may complain about it (s 124A(1))`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` FALSE FALSE `race` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `not covered: section 124A reaches only a public act`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE TRUE `race` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `no: distributing matter whose content the person did not know, and could not reasonably be expected to know, is not a public act (s 124A(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `age` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `not covered: section 124A reaches only vilification on the ground of race, religion, sexuality, sex characteristics or gender identity`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `impairment` TRUE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `not covered: section 124A reaches only vilification on the ground of race, religion, sexuality, sex characteristics or gender identity`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `gender identity` FALSE `none of the excepted kinds` EQUALS `not covered: section 124A reaches only an act that incites hatred towards, serious contempt for, or severe ridicule of a person or group`
#ASSERT `Was I vilified` TRUE FALSE `sexuality` TRUE `the publication of a fair report of a public act` EQUALS `no: section 124A(2) does not make it unlawful: a fair report, absolutely privileged material, or an act done reasonably and in good faith for academic, artistic, scientific, research or public interest purposes`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `chapter 5`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the advertisement unlawful` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the advertisement contravenes s 127(1), and you may complain about it`
#ASSERT `Is the advertisement unlawful` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: an advertisement for a worker under 21 years of age, so far as it advertises for one, is outside s 127(1) (s 127(1A))`
#ASSERT `Is the advertisement unlawful` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the respondent has a defence to your complaint: it proves it took reasonable precautions to prevent the publication or display (s 127(2))`
#ASSERT `Is the advertisement unlawful` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 127 reaches only an advertisement indicating an intention to act in a way that contravenes the Act`

#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `because I, or someone associated with or related to me, is, has been or intends to be involved in a proceeding under the Act`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `because I, or someone associated with or related to me, in good faith alleged or intends to allege a contravention of the Act`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `because the person believes I, or someone associated with or related to me, did, is doing or intends to do one of those things`
#ASSERT `Was I victimised` TRUE `because I, or someone associated with or related to me, refused to do an act that would contravene the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I victimised` TRUE `because I, or someone associated with or related to me, alleged a contravention of the Act, but not in good faith`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I victimised` TRUE `for another reason`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Was I victimised` FALSE `because I, or someone associated with or related to me, is, has been or intends to be involved in a proceeding under the Act`)

#ASSERT (`What is the most the person who victimised me can be penalised` FALSE)'s `the penalty units` EQUALS 45
#ASSERT (`What is the most the person who victimised me can be penalised` FALSE)'s `the months of imprisonment` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`What is the most the person who victimised me can be penalised` TRUE)'s `the penalty units` EQUALS 170
#ASSERT (`What is the most the person who victimised me can be penalised` TRUE)'s `the months of imprisonment` EQUALS 0

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 133`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Is the employer liable too` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the employer or principal and its worker or agent are jointly and severally liable, and you may complain against either or both (s 133(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the employer liable too` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the employer or principal has a defence, having proved it took reasonable steps to prevent the contravention (s 133(2)); the worker or agent remains liable`
#ASSERT `Is the employer liable too` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 133 applies only to a contravention by a worker or agent in the course of work or while acting as agent`
#ASSERT `Is the employer liable too` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 133 applies only to a contravention by a worker or agent in the course of work or while acting as agent`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `making a complaint`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `the person subjected to the alleged contravention` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may complain to the Human Rights Commissioner (s 134(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `an agent of that person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may complain to the Human Rights Commissioner (s 134(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `a person authorised in writing by the commissioner to act for a person who was subjected to it and cannot make or authorise a complaint` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may complain to the Human Rights Commissioner (s 134(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `a body whose primary purpose is promoting the interests or welfare of people of a particular race, religion, sexuality, gender identity or sex characteristics` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the body may complain about the vilification, and the commissioner may accept the complaint (s 134(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `a body whose primary purpose is promoting the interests or welfare of people of a particular race, religion, sexuality, gender identity or sex characteristics` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the commissioner may accept the body's complaint only if satisfied it is made in good faith, about conduct that has affected or is likely to affect the people the body serves, and in the interests of justice (s 134(4))`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `a body whose primary purpose is promoting the interests or welfare of people of a particular race, religion, sexuality, gender identity or sex characteristics` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not covered: section 134(3) lets such a body complain only about vilification under s 124A`
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint` `someone else` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: section 134 does not name you among the people who may complain`

#ASSERT `Is my complaint in the proper form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my complaint in the proper form` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my complaint in the proper form` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Does my agreement not to complain stop my complaint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the commissioner may accept your complaint despite the agreement, being of the reasonable opinion that it is fair to (s 137(1))`
#ASSERT `Does my agreement not to complain stop my complaint` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the commissioner is not of the opinion that accepting it is fair, and a decision not to accept it is a rejection: the complaint lapses and you cannot complain again about the same act or omission (ss 137(1), 142(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Does my agreement not to complain stop my complaint` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: you made no agreement not to complain, so s 137 does not arise`

-- s 138: 1 year after 15 March 2026 is 15 March 2027; after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I make my complaint` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint is made within 1 year of every contravention it alleges (s 138(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint is made more than 1 year after the contravention and no good cause is shown, so it is not accepted; that is a rejection, and you cannot complain again about the same act or omission (ss 138(2)(b), 142(1), (4))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) (`d` 16 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `late, but it may be accepted: the commissioner is satisfied you have shown good cause (s 138(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 28 2 2029) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint is made within 1 year of every contravention it alleges (s 138(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint is made more than 1 year after the contravention and no good cause is shown, so it is not accepted; that is a rejection, and you cannot complain again about the same act or omission (ss 138(2)(b), 142(1), (4))`
-- a series from 1 February 2026 to 1 June 2026: complained 1 February 2027 (all in time), 15 March 2027 (partly), 2 June 2027 (all late)
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint is made within 1 year of every contravention it alleges (s 138(1))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `partly: the contraventions within the year are in time; the earlier ones are not accepted, as no good cause is shown, though the commissioner may defer that decision until after conciliation (ss 138(2)(b), 141A, 142(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `partly: the contraventions within the year are in time; the earlier ones may also be accepted, as you have shown good cause, and the commissioner may defer that decision until after conciliation (ss 138(2)(a), 141A)`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS `partly: the contraventions within the year are in time; the earlier ones are not accepted, as no good cause is shown, though the commissioner may defer that decision until after conciliation (ss 138(2)(b), 141A, 142(4), (5))`
#ASSERT `Is my complaint in time` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) (`d` 2 6 2027) TRUE EQUALS `late, but it may be accepted: the commissioner is satisfied you have shown good cause (s 138(2)(a))`

#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, it must be: the commissioner is of the reasonable opinion that it is frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 139); it lapses and you cannot complain again about the same act or omission (s 142(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it may be rejected or stayed: there are concurrent proceedings in a court or tribunal, or another entity may deal with it effectively or conveniently (s 140(1)); time limits do not run while it is stayed (s 140(3)), and a rejected complaint lapses (s 142(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it may be rejected or stayed: there are concurrent proceedings in a court or tribunal, or another entity may deal with it effectively or conveniently (s 140(1)); time limits do not run while it is stayed (s 140(3)), and a rejected complaint lapses (s 142(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `it may be rejected: another entity has adequately dealt with the act or omission (s 140(2)); a rejected complaint lapses (s 142(1))`
#ASSERT `Can my complaint be rejected` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: neither s 139 nor s 140 gives a ground to reject it`

#ASSERT `By when must the commissioner decide whether to accept my complaint` (`d` 10 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2028
#ASSERT `By when must the commissioner decide whether to accept my complaint` (`d` 10 2 2027) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2027

#ASSERT `By when can I ask for reasons for the rejection` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 17 1 2027
#ASSERT `Am I in time to ask for reasons for the rejection` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 17 1 2027)
#ASSERT `Am I in time to ask for reasons for the rejection` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 20 12 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I in time to ask for reasons for the rejection` (`d` 20 12 2026) (`d` 18 1 2027))

#ASSERT `If I was dismissed, can I complain and seek industrial relief` TRUE `I applied for industrial relief before lodging my complaint` EQUALS `you may proceed with both, but the tribunal cannot order your reinstatement or re-employment on the complaint (s 154)`
#ASSERT `If I was dismissed, can I complain and seek industrial relief` TRUE `I lodged my complaint and was notified it was accepted, without having applied for industrial relief` EQUALS `you may only proceed with the complaint, and cannot later apply for industrial relief for the same circumstances (s 153)`
#ASSERT `If I was dismissed, can I complain and seek industrial relief` TRUE `I lodged my complaint, then applied for industrial relief before being notified it was accepted` EQUALS `not covered: neither s 153 nor s 154 applies where industrial relief is sought after the complaint is lodged but before notice that it was accepted`
#ASSERT `If I was dismissed, can I complain and seek industrial relief` TRUE `I have done neither yet` EQUALS `you choose: applying for industrial relief first keeps both, but the tribunal then cannot order reinstatement or re-employment (s 154); lodging the complaint and being notified it is accepted first loses industrial relief (s 153)`
#ASSERT `If I was dismissed, can I complain and seek industrial relief` FALSE `I applied for industrial relief before lodging my complaint` EQUALS `not covered: sections 153 and 154 apply only to a worker dismissed in circumstances giving both a complaint and industrial relief`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `conciliation and referral`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Which tribunal will hear my complaint` TRUE EQUALS `the Queensland Industrial Relations Commission: the complaint is or includes a work-related matter (schedule 1; ss 164A(2)(a), 166(1)(a), 167(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Which tribunal will hear my complaint` FALSE EQUALS `the Queensland Civil and Administrative Tribunal (QCAT): the complaint is not a work-related matter (schedule 1; ss 164A(2)(b), 166(1)(b), 167(1)(b))`

#ASSERT `What can happen if I miss the conciliation conference` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the commissioner may dismiss your complaint and direct you to pay the respondent's costs, which the respondent can enforce through a court (s 160(1), (3), (4))`
#ASSERT `What can happen if I miss the conciliation conference` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: section 160(1) applies only if you, without reasonable excuse, do not comply with a direction to attend`
#ASSERT `What can happen if I miss the conciliation conference` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 160(1) applies only if you, without reasonable excuse, do not comply with a direction to attend`
#ASSERT `What can happen if I miss the conciliation conference` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 160(1) applies only if you, without reasonable excuse, do not comply with a direction to attend`

#ASSERT `Is our settlement enforceable as a tribunal order` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our settlement enforceable as a tribunal order` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is our settlement enforceable as a tribunal order` FALSE TRUE)

#ASSERT `Can I require referral after the conciliation conference` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: by written notice to the commissioner, at any time; the commissioner must promptly refer it to the tribunal, unless the commissioner acts under s 168 because the complaint is frivolous or lacking in substance (s 164A(2) to (4))`
#ASSERT `Can I require referral after the conciliation conference` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: once the commissioner has given notice that the complaint cannot be resolved by conciliation, s 164A stops applying; you may require referral under s 166 within 28 days of that notice (s 165(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I require referral after the conciliation conference` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: once the commissioner has given notice that the complaint cannot be resolved by conciliation, s 164A stops applying; you may require referral under s 166 within 28 days of that notice (s 165(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I require referral after the conciliation conference` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint was resolved by conciliation; the agreement is enforceable once recorded, signed and filed (s 164)`
#ASSERT `Can I require referral after the conciliation conference` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: section 164A applies only after a conciliation conference has been held`

-- s 166: notified 1 March 2027; the 28th day is 29 March 2027
-- no extension asked
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2027
-- asked on 10 March, refused by notice on 15 March: 10 to 15 March (6 days) not counted, so 4 April 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 4 4 2027
-- asked on the same day as the refusal (10 March): 1 day not counted, 30 March 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2027) (`d` 10 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 11 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 3 2027
-- asked on the last day (29 March), refused by notice on Friday 9 April: 12 days not counted gives Saturday 10 April;
-- s 166(4) gives the next business day, Monday 12 April 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 9 4 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 12 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 4 2027
-- asked on the 29th day, too late for s 166(2)(a): the 28th day stands
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 3 2027) (`d` 5 4 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 6 4 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2027
-- granted to 30 April 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I require referral after the conciliation notice` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2027) (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2027) (`d` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 4 2027

#ASSERT `From when can I ask for referral because the complaint is taking too long` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 7 2027
#ASSERT `From when can I ask for referral because the complaint is taking too long` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `From when can I ask for referral because the complaint is taking too long` (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 4 2027

-- s 167(4): the commissioner asked on 1 March 2027
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the complaint is referred: you agreed in writing in time, so the commissioner must refer it to the tribunal (s 167(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 3 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the complaint lapses: you did not agree in writing in time, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission (s 167(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the complaint lapses: you did not agree in writing in time, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission (s 167(4)(c))`
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 4 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2027) EQUALS `the complaint is referred: you agreed in writing in time, so the commissioner must refer it to the tribunal (s 167(4)(b))`
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 16 4 2027) TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2027) EQUALS `the complaint lapses: you did not agree in writing in time, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission (s 167(4)(c))`
-- an extension given without a request in time is not one s 167(4)(d) allows: the 28 days stand
#ASSERT `If the respondent asks for referral, does my complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 4 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2027) EQUALS `the complaint lapses: you did not agree in writing in time, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission (s 167(4)(c))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `lapse and withdrawal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `By when must I answer the lapse notice` `a notice that I appear to have lost interest in the complaint (s 169)` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must I answer the lapse notice` `a show cause notice that another entity has dealt, or may better deal, with the complaint (s 168A)` (`d` 10 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2028

#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice that I appear to have lost interest in the complaint (s 169)` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 29 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint does not lapse under this section, and the commissioner deals with it`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice that I appear to have lost interest in the complaint (s 169)` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 30 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint lapses, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice that I appear to have lost interest in the complaint (s 169)` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint lapses, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice given after I said I do not want to continue with the complaint (s 170)` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `no: the complaint does not lapse under this section, and the commissioner deals with it`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice given after I said I do not want to continue with the complaint (s 170)` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the complaint lapses, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission`
-- s 168 and s 168A turn on the commissioner's view at the end of the 28 days, whatever the answer (finding 5)
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice that my complaint appears frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 168)` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2027) TRUE EQUALS `yes: the complaint lapses, and you cannot make a further complaint about the same act or omission`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a notice that my complaint appears frivolous, trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance (s 168)` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint does not lapse under this section, and the commissioner deals with it`
#ASSERT `Does my complaint lapse after the notice` `a show cause notice that another entity has dealt, or may better deal, with the complaint (s 168A)` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint does not lapse under this section, and the commissioner deals with it`

#ASSERT `On what day does my withdrawn complaint lapse` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 3 2027

#ASSERT `Can I have the lapse reviewed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `yes: you applied in time; if the tribunal is satisfied you have a genuine interest in continuing, the commissioner must resume dealing with the complaint (s 169(3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can I have the lapse reviewed` (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `no: the 28 days after notice of the lapse have passed (s 169(3))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `before the tribunal`
-- ===================================================================================================================

#ASSERT `Can I ask for an order protecting my complaint` `with the commissioner, not yet referred` EQUALS `yes: before referral you may apply to the tribunal for an order stopping a person from doing an act that might prejudice the investigation, the conciliation or a later order; it may be heard without the respondent if the interests of justice require (s 144(1), (3))`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an order protecting my complaint` `referred to the tribunal, not yet decided` EQUALS `yes: after referral and before the decision you may apply for an order stopping a person from doing an act that might prejudice an order the tribunal might make (s 190(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I ask for an order protecting my complaint` `decided by the tribunal` EQUALS `no: sections 144 and 190 apply only until the tribunal decides the complaint`

#ASSERT `Will the tribunal deal with my complaint` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `yes: the tribunal must accept it, as the complaint was made within 1 year of the alleged contravention (s 175(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the tribunal deal with my complaint` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 2 2 2027) TRUE EQUALS `yes: the complaint was made more than 1 year after the contravention, but the tribunal considers it reasonable, on the balance of fairness between the parties, to deal with it (s 175(2))`
#ASSERT `Will the tribunal deal with my complaint` (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 2 2 2027) FALSE EQUALS `no: the complaint was made more than 1 year after the contravention, and the tribunal does not consider it reasonable, on the balance of fairness, to deal with it (s 175(2))`

#ASSERT `Who must prove what at the hearing` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the respondent is taken to have contravened the Act: there are facts from which that could be decided, absent any other explanation, and the respondent has not proved it did not (s 204(1), (2)); any exemption is for the respondent to prove (s 205)`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what at the hearing` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the respondent proved, on the balance of probabilities, that it did not contravene the Act (s 204(2))`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what at the hearing` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 204(1) does not help you: there are no facts from which a contravention could be decided absent any other explanation`
#ASSERT `Who must prove what at the hearing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the former sections 204 to 206 apply, as in force before 1 December 2024 (s 285AA); their text is not in the deposited version, so this encoding cannot say more`

#ASSERT `What orders can the tribunal make for me` FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an order dismissing the complaint (s 210)`
#ASSERT `What orders can the tribunal make for me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `an order not to commit a further contravention against you (s 209(1)(a))`, `compensation for your loss or damage, including offence, embarrassment, humiliation and intimidation, paid within a set period, with no cap in the Act (s 209(1)(b), (6))`, `an order to do specified things to redress your loss or damage, such as employing, reinstating, re-employing or promoting you (s 209(1)(c), (4))`, `a private apology or retraction (s 209(1)(d))`, `a public apology or retraction (s 209(1)(e))`, `an order to implement programs to eliminate unlawful discrimination (s 209(1)(f))`, `interest on the compensation (s 209(1)(g))`, `an order declaring void all or part of an agreement made in connection with the contravention (s 209(1)(h))`
#ASSERT `What orders can the tribunal make for me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `an order not to commit a further contravention against you (s 209(1)(a))`, `compensation for your loss or damage, including offence, embarrassment, humiliation and intimidation, paid within a set period, with no cap in the Act (s 209(1)(b), (6))`, `an order to do specified things to redress your loss or damage, but not to reinstate or re-employ you (ss 154, 209(1)(c), (4))`, `a private apology or retraction (s 209(1)(d))`, `a public apology or retraction (s 209(1)(e))`, `an order to implement programs to eliminate unlawful discrimination (s 209(1)(f))`, `interest on the compensation (s 209(1)(g))`, `an order declaring void all or part of an agreement made in connection with the contravention (s 209(1)(h))`
